From 27149d3989b61aea0cab2aa0676b2756d858584f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:03:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] pmre-kit: optional std feature so the kit builds no_std +
 alloc

The kit's mechanism needs nothing from std, so make std an opt-out
feature (on by default, existing users unaffected):

- no_std + alloc when `std` is off; a crate prelude supplies the alloc
  types, and `fmath::F32Ext` the float methods core lacks (floor, ceil,
  round, trunc, sqrt, sin, cos, rem_euclid), tested against std.
- `sync`: std's Arc/Mutex/OnceLock/HashMap with std; a spin Mutex,
  once-cell and BTreeMap without it. The layout measure memo uses a
  thread-local with std and a locked map without.
- font: `font::install(regular, bold)` installs faces from bytes (the
  only font source without std); system discovery is std-only.
- text: `draw_face` / `advance_face` render with an explicit face (e.g.
  a monospace font) through the same coverage path.
- path: fill/stroke are generic over `Surface`, like scan_convert and
  text, so they can target any pixel sink.
- post, bloom_sweep and fair_queue (threads) are std-only.
- CI also clippy-checks the kit without std on x86_64-unknown-none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
