+### Without `std` (operating systems, firmware)
+
+`pmre-kit` has a default `std` feature. Disable it to build the kit as `no_std` + `alloc`
+(any target with a global allocator):
+
+```toml
+pmre-kit = { git = "https://github.com/Lucerna-Labs/atom-rendering-engine.git", rev = "FULL_COMMIT_SHA", default-features = false }
+```
+
+Without `std` there is no system-font discovery: parse embedded TrueType bytes and install
+them before drawing text, e.g. `font::install(Font::parse(REGULAR_TTF.to_vec())?, bold)`.
+`text::draw_face` draws with any other parsed face (such as a monospace one). The threaded
+modules (`post`, `bloom_sweep`, `fair_queue`) are `std`-only; shapes, paths, gradients,
+text, layout and HTML all work unchanged, rendering into any `Surface` you implement.
+Atom OS uses this mode for its desktop.
+
 ## 3. Render a first frame
 
 The UXI path is the shortest route to a laid-out 2D interface:
